B.QM=new A.iB("xPts","Expected points","How many FPL points we think a player will score.","Not a prediction of what will happen \u2014 an average of what would happen if the same fixture were played many times. A striker with 5.0 xPts might blank or haul; over a season, backing the higher number wins.","Per gameweek: under 3 is bench material, 4\u20135 is a solid starter, above 6 is premium.")
B.QO=new A.iB("FDR","Fixture Difficulty Rating","How hard a single match is, from 1 to 5.","Green is easy, red is hard. It reflects the opponent's strength and whether the match is home or away \u2014 the same opponent is rated harder away from home. Where a run of matches is rated, the number is the average across them, so it stays on the same 1\u20135 scale as one match.","1\u20132 is a good run, 3 is neutral, 4\u20135 is one to avoid or sell into.")
B.QN=new A.iB("Ceiling","How big the good weeks get","How much of a projection comes from goals, assists and bonus rather than from turning up and keeping a clean sheet.","Two players on the same expected points are not the same bet. A defender's 5.0 is mostly appearance and clean sheet points, which stop there; a striker's 5.0 can be a blank or a fifteen. That gap matters most for the armband, which doubles the swing as well as the score, so the captain ranking is tilted toward it \u2014 a goalkeeper can sit below a forward who projects fewer points.","High ceiling: over half the projection is goals, assists and bonus. Mid: about a third. Low: mostly points that cap out.")
B.QH=new A.iB("Crowding","Template, balanced or differential","Whether captaining this player follows the crowd or breaks from it.","Neither is better on its own \u2014 it depends on what you are chasing. Captaining the template is a shield: if they haul, you keep pace, and if they blank, so does everyone. Captaining a differential is a swing, and swings work in both directions. What you should not do is take one without knowing which you took.","Template: owned by 20% or more, or the most-captained player. Balanced: 5\u201320%. Differential: under 5%.")
B.QJ=new A.iB("FCPS","Fantasy Composite Player Score","One 0\u20131000 number blending recent form, fixtures, season points and involvement, for ranking players against each other.","Four measures, each scored against the highest player in the game and then weighted: form 40%, fixture difficulty over the next three 25%, total points 20%, and ICT index 15%. Difficulty is inverted, so an easy run pushes the score up.\n\nIt is a ranking, not a quantity of points. FCPS 700 does not mean 700 of anything and cannot be weighed against a -4 hit \u2014 use xPts for that. What it is good at is the question xPts answers less directly: who is worth a look right now, given how they are playing and who they are about to face.","A ranking, not a threshold. Nobody approaches 1000 \u2014 that would mean leading the whole game on points, form, involvement and fixtures at once \u2014 so compare players against each other rather than a fixed bar. Before a ball is kicked no one has any form, which is 40% of the score, and the whole table compresses.")
B.QF=new A.iB("EO","Effective ownership","The share of rivals who will get points from a player this week.","Counts captaincy, so it can exceed 100%: a player owned by half your league and captained by all of them is 100% effective ownership. It is what decides whether a haul gains you rank or merely keeps you level.","Above 50% is a template pick \u2014 not owning him is the active risk.")
B.QG=new A.iB("xGI","Expected goal involvements","Expected goals and assists combined \u2014 chances created and taken.","Measures the quality of chances a player gets into, rather than whether they went in. It steadies faster than actual goals, so it spots form earlier and survives a cold finishing run.",null)
B.QI=new A.iB("PPG","Points per game","A player's average FPL points across the matches they played.","Ignores games missed, so it flatters someone who has been injured for most of the season. Read it next to minutes, not on its own.",null)
B.QE=new A.iB("GW","Gameweek","One round of Premier League fixtures, and one FPL scoring period.","Transfers and chips lock at the deadline, roughly 90 minutes before the first match of the round.",null)
B.QK=new A.iB("BGW","Blank gameweek","A round where some clubs have no fixture, so their players score 0.","Caused by cup competitions taking league dates. The usual answer is a Free Hit, or planning transfers a week or two ahead of it.",null)
B.QL=new A.iB("DGW","Double gameweek","A round where some clubs play twice, so their players score twice.","The best week to use Bench Boost or Triple Captain, because every player involved gets two bites at the same chip.",null)
B.nY=new A.bK(B.Zb,[B.QM,B.QO,B.QN,B.QH,B.QJ,B.QF,B.QG,B.QI,B.QE,B.QK,B.QL],A.ax("bK<h,iB>"))
